"Usage: someip_subscriber [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --uauthority <UAUTHORITY>\n          Authority for the local subscriber identity [default: authority-b]\n      --uentity <UENTITY>\n          UEntity ID for local subscriber identity (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x15BB0]\n      --uversion <UVERSION>\n          UEntity major version for local subscriber identity (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x1]\n      --resource <RESOURCE>\n          Resource ID for local subscriber identity (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x0]\n      --source-authority <SOURCE_AUTHORITY>\n          Source authority filter for publish subscription [default: authority-b]\n      --source-uentity <SOURCE_UENTITY>\n          Source UEntity ID filter for publish subscription (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x13039]\n      --source-uversion <SOURCE_UVERSION>\n          Source UEntity major version filter for publish subscription (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x1]\n      --source-resource <SOURCE_RESOURCE>\n          Source resource ID filter for publish subscription (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x8001]\n      --remote-authority <REMOTE_AUTHORITY>\n          Remote authority used by the SOME/IP transport bridge [default: authority-b]\n      --vsomeip-config <VSOMEIP_CONFIG>\n          Path to the vsomeip JSON configuration file [default: <example-dir>/vsomeip-configs/someip_subscriber.json]\n      --encoding <ENCODING>\n          Payload encoding fixed by the SOME/IP topic convention [default: protobuf] [possible values: native, protobuf, xcdrv2, arrow, omgidl]\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n"
